{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbfQKBx5355aE1gU6do4", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here's a regex for an ISO 8601 calendar date (`YYYY-MM-DD`):\n\n```\n^\\d{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])$\n```\n\n- `\\d{4}` is the four-digit year.\n- `(0[1-9]|1[0-2])` is the month, 01\u201312.\n- `(0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])` is the day, 01\u201331.\n- `^` and `$` anchor the match to the whole string. To find dates inside longer text, replace them with `\\b`.\n\nIt checks the format and the ranges of the month and day. It doesn't check that the day exists in that month, so `2026-02-31` still matches. Leap years aren't checked either. For real validation, parse the string with a date library after the regex match."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7225, "cache_read_input_tokens": 16780, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7225}, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "aa00b91c-5e9f-48c9-8bd2-a0c7ef7d2f3e", "uuid": "76a4bbdf-f60f-4a39-8ee2-d68506314f72", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T14:19:15.170Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbfQJr7TDJwJt5ZPxMmS"}
